    },
    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: '31 (Scat)',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '31 (Scat) is a knock game. Get 31 points in one suit (A=11, face=10, number=face value) or highest three-card hand. Draw one, discard one. Knock when confident; lowest hand loses a life. Blitz: 31 in three cards declared immediately; others lose a life. Last player with lives wins.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Probably descended from the 15th-century Italian gambling game trente et un; later popular in France, England and Ireland. The modern 31 / Scat variant is widely played in America and Britain under names like Blitz, Cadillac and Ride the Bus.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two or more players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck. Aces count 11, court cards 10, other cards face value. Dutch variant (Eenendertigen) uses a 32-card pack (7 and above).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '52-card deck, 3-4 lives per player',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '3 cards each; one card up for discard; rest stock.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: "California Quick: Fast-running home game variant where ties for lowest hand during a knock can cost the knocker two lives, and an opening knock on the first turn ('knocking out of the gate') ends the round immediately.",
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Banking: Banked version where everyone antes to a central pot and a special three-card widow can be exchanged with; highest hand or blitz (exact 31) wins the pot instead of simply losing lives.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Dollar bill: American scoring variant where each player tracks lives by folding the corners of a banknote; losing a life folds a corner and the last player with an unfolded bill wins the stake.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
